Template Pack · doc-spine

These files are skeletons for a new project. Copy them to your target project:

  templates/CLAUDE.md         →  <PROJECT>/CLAUDE.md
  templates/README.md         →  <PROJECT>/README.md
  templates/HOWTO.md          →  <PROJECT>/HOWTO.md
  templates/STATE.md          →  <PROJECT>/instances/<ACTIVE_INSTANCE>/STATE.md
  templates/INSTANCE_README.md → <PROJECT>/instances/<ACTIVE_INSTANCE>/README.md
  templates/TASKS.md          →  <PROJECT>/instances/<ACTIVE_INSTANCE>/docs/TASKS.md
  templates/ROADMAP.md        →  <PROJECT>/docs/ROADMAP.md
  templates/CONVENTIONS.md    →  <PROJECT>/docs/CONVENTIONS.md

Note · the relative links inside these templates (e.g., `../STATE.md`, `docs/TASKS.md`, `../../docs/ROADMAP.md`) intentionally do NOT resolve from this `templates/` directory — they are designed to resolve once the file is in its target location in the new project.

Placeholders to fill in:
  <PROJECT_NAME>           project name
  <PROJECT_PATH>           memory directory path (e.g., -Users-yourname-work-myproject)
  <ACTIVE_INSTANCE>        active instance directory name
  <DOMAIN-SPECIFIC-RULE>   any domain-specific rule for your project
  <REGISTRY>               if you have a pure registry, e.g., HPC_inventory

Optional next:
  - Add `.aiignore` to any frozen / read-only instance directory
  - Add a domain-specific entry to CONVENTIONS.md §6
  - When a pivot-heavy phase begins: cp templates/INDEX.md → instances/<ACTIVE_INSTANCE>/scratch/INDEX.md
    (catalog for non-canonical exploration drafts; see SPEC §8.4). Not needed at bootstrap.
